    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0493" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg453"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1509.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">
                                August</hi> 12, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The Secretary of the Navy has communicated
                    to this department a despatch of the 24th ultimo, addressed to him by
                    Rear-Admiral Goldsborough, from Flushing, which is accompanied by a copy of a
                    letter addressed to him by you, which appears to be in answer to one from the
                    admiral, in which he asked whether the British government still adhered to the
                    application of the twenty-four-hour rule to the departure of our Vessels being
                    found with them at the time of their arrival. Admiral Goldsborough asks whether,
                    under the circumstances set forth in your letter, he is still to avoid the ports
                    of England, and still decline to exchange courtesies and ceremonies with her
                    naval and other authorities. To this inquiry this department has, under the
                    instructions of the President, requested Mr. Welles to reply in the
                    affirmative.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
